Realignment events to analyze: 5419 

Distribution of number of ties changed at realignment:

   1    3 
5414    5 

Events with exactly one tie changed: 5414 of 5419 (99.9%)

=== Data feature: embeddedness is tied across a triad's 3 edges far more than expected ===
All three tied: 74.6 %
Exactly 2 tied: 22.6 %
All 3 distinct: 2.7 %
(This happens because triads embedded in a dense alliance bloc share most of their
 common neighbors across all three edges simultaneously -- a real structural feature
 of alliance blocs, not a data artifact. It means a naive 'is this tie tied for the
 min' test is dominated by degenerate 3-way ties and is not a meaningful ranking test.)

=== H2, naive test (counts ties as 'success'): was the changed tie tied for the minimum? ===
Observed: 82.9 % (null = 33.3% if chosen at random)

	Exact binomial test

data:  sum(single$is_min, na.rm = TRUE) and sum(!is.na(single$is_min))
number of successes = 4488, number of trials = 5414, p-value < 2.2e-16
alternative hypothesis: true probability of success is not equal to 0.3333333
95 percent confidence interval:
 0.818663 0.838905
sample estimates:
probability of success 
              0.828962 


