=== H2, betweenness version (much better powered: n=1781 with all 3 distinct) ===
Observed: changed tie has the MINIMUM betweenness in 24 % of events (null = 33.3%)

	Exact binomial test

data:  sum(strict_b$is_min_btw) and nrow(strict_b)
number of successes = 428, number of trials = 1781, p-value < 2.2e-16
alternative hypothesis: true probability of success is not equal to 0.3333333
95 percent confidence interval:
 0.2206308 0.2608571
sample estimates:
probability of success 
             0.2403144 

This is significantly BELOW chance: realignment concentrates on the tie with the
HIGHEST, not lowest, betweenness within the triad -- the opposite of H2 as stated.

